(6157821, 899696, 104809, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by david_c:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by zencow:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a great picture... but, what do you mean by "Post processing includes cleaning up a little lens-flare"?   Is that allowed under the Basic Editing rules?  just curious.  :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Lens-flare, but I have a feeling you''re being sarcastic. I suppose, since it has not yet been validated by the SC, that it could still be DQ''ed. :( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m sorry, David.  I really didn''t mean to come off that way.  I did suspect it might not have been allowed, but I''m new around here and was honestly just trying to learn something more about what you can and can''t do in Basic.  I''m _not_ happy that your shot was DQ''d.  I really like the picture.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-09-09 19:27:28.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by david_c: Originally posted by zencow: It''s a great picture... but, what do you mean by "Post processing includes cleaning up a little lens-flare"?   Is that allowed under the Basic Editing rules?  just curious.  :)  Lens-flare, but I have a feeling you''re being sarcastic. I suppose, since it has not yet been validated by the SC, that it could still be DQ''ed. :(   I''m sorry, David.  I really didn''t mean to come off that way.  I did suspect it might not have been allowed, but I''m new around here and was honestly just trying to learn something more about what you can and can''t do in Basic.  I''m _not_ happy that your shot was DQ''d.  I really like the picture.', '2010-09-09 20:22:41.000000', '2010-09-09 20:27:28.000000', 0),
